:: dialog/kai/backstory-1 [dialog kai]
Kai — Former Lab Technician
"I remember now. The city sealed overnight.
We were mid-experiment."

:: dialog/kai/backstory-2 [dialog kai]
"Whatever you used... it worked. I've been
looping for weeks. Trapped in that corner."

"I know this city's systems. I want out too."

:: dialog/kai/backstory-3 [dialog kai]
"Tell me what you need. I'll help."

[Kai hands you a Lab Keycard and a Compound Sample.]
[Kai joins your cause. They are waiting for you at Apartment 4B.]

:: dialog/kai/to-player-first [dialog kai]
Kai studies you for a long moment.
"You haven't said a word since you woke me.
Do you even have a voice?"
---
"...I wasn't sure. Until now."

Your own voice. Rusted from disuse.
The first words spoken in the sealed city.
---
Kai nods slowly, as if that settled something.
"Then we can start telling each other the truth."

:: dialog/kai/to-player-again [dialog kai]
"Still not much of a talker. That's fine.
The city says enough for both of you."

:: dialog/kai/to-maren [dialog kai]
"Maren. You kept the community room going."

"Kept it counted, anyway. You're the lab one —
Kai, right? You people never bought from us.
Everything came in on the company trucks."
---
Kai is quiet for a moment.
"Those trucks stopped a week before the sirens.
I remember thinking that was strange."

:: dialog/kai/waiting [dialog kai]
"I'm ready when you are.
This city won't explain itself."
